<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!-- InteractionTask: the one thread on which this player POSTs a viewer's press
     back to the relay (POST /player/v1/interaction — interactive slide layers,
     parity milestones 1.5/3.7). An HTTP round trip cannot happen on the render
     thread: roUrlTransfer's wait() would block every Label, every Video and the
     D-pad itself for the duration, so a screen would visibly freeze each time
     somebody pressed a button on it.

     EXACTLY ONE of these exists, created once by PhotonScene and never
     re-created — the same rule IdleDefeatTask states and for the same reason:
     Task threads survive the removal of the node that owns them, and this fleet
     has already halted a channel by hitting the firmware thread cap with
     per-event Tasks. The legacy player created a fresh ApiTask per press, which
     is precisely that shape; a wall panel somebody presses a few hundred times a
     day would reach the cap on its own.

     Fields:
       press    — the scene writes one {lease_id, interaction, slide_id} press
                  here. A field WRITE is the queue: this task observes the field
                  through a message port, so a press posted while a previous one
                  is still in flight is delivered by the port rather than lost.
       stopFlag — cooperative shutdown; PhotonScene.shutdown() sets it and the
                  loop returns at its next wake-up.

     Storage/Http are included explicitly because SceneGraph component scopes do
     not inherit pkg:/source globals. Pairing.brs is deliberately NOT included
     even though Http.brs calls its wvStr: pulling it in would drag the whole
     pairing/crypto chain (Base32, Asn1, PairCode, Commitment) into a thread that
     posts one small JSON body. InteractionTask.brs defines wvStr itself instead,
     which satisfies Http.brs from this component's own flat scope. The relay address, the channel token and
     the pinned trust anchor are read from persisted state HERE rather than
     passed down from the scene: they are credentials, the scene has no other use
     for them, and reading them at press time means a re-paired player posts to
     the relay it is paired to NOW. -->
<component name="InteractionTask" extends="Task">
  <interface>
    <field id="press" type="assocarray" />
    <field id="stopFlag" type="boolean" value="false" />
  </interface>
  <script type="text/brightscript" uri="pkg:/components/InteractionTask.brs" />
  <script type="text/brightscript" uri="pkg:/source/Storage.brs" />
  <script type="text/brightscript" uri="pkg:/source/Http.brs" />
</component>
